    "profile_text": {
        "body": "Workday is a public company, traded as WDAY, founded in 2005 and headquartered in Pleasanton, California. Its own site presents it as an enterprise AI platform for HR, finance, and IT, and describes a product line it calls Workday AI, covering HR and finance AI, skills-based talent, and predictive analytics. The company says its agents can find, build, act, and automate across those functions, and it markets the offering around trust, agility, and data readiness. It also points to Sana and agentic AI as part of how it describes a new way to work.\n\nThe company's most recent annual filing is a 10-K for a period ending January 31, 2026, reporting revenue of $9,552,000,000. Its SEC Central Index Key is 0001327811.\n\nCourt records associated with Workday include 281 cases in California. Named suits listed in federal district courts include Meckfessel Poletti v. Workday, Inc. in the E.D. California, Williams v. Workday, Inc. in the N.D. Georgia, Elias v. Workday, Inc. in the N.D. California, Noriega (PS) v. Workday, Inc. and Doe (PS) v. Workday, Inc. in the D. Colorado, and Hill v. Workday, Inc. in the D. Maryland and E.D. Virginia.",
